  "details": "<p>This\u00a0<span class=\"highlightedSearchTerm\">archive</span>\u00a0is located in the\u00a0Northwest Palace.</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0<img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"368\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan66_general_plan_Kalhu1-17_p144.png\" width=\"399\" /></p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"569\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan69_northwest_palace_Kalhu6-11_p149.png\" width=\"432\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Most documents found in the Northwest Palace, built by the Assyrian king Ashurnarsipal II (883\u2013859 BC), predate the move of the new Assyrian capital to Dur-\u0160arrukin under Sargon II (721\u2013705 BC). Fourteen clay tablets and sealings, dating from 719 to 715 BC, were found in Room HH, in the southeastern part of the palace.",
